                                "sense_id": "834c8751-365d-3225-a098-1eb843afb083",
                                "text": "an arborous landscape; arborous vegetation"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2fd66b08-b0d0-4c73-b627-b622deee1a66",
                                "sense_id": "834c8751-365d-3225-a098-1eb843afb083",
                                "text": "[…] from under shadie arborous roof,\nSoon as they forth were come to open sight\nOf day-spring,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca8edf60-3d4a-49d9-a3f6-e379c4fc10a6",
                                "sense_id": "834c8751-365d-3225-a098-1eb843afb083",
                                "text": "1797, Samuel Taylor Coleridge, “Dedication to the Reverend George Coleridge” in Poems, Bristol: J. Cottle, 2nd edition, pp. x-xi,\n[…] the Tree […] whose old boughs,\nThat hang above us in an arborous roof,\nStirr’d by the faint gale of departing May\nSend their loose blossoms slanting o’er our heads!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9275e774-ce2d-44b7-8c4b-35397b796f28",
                                "sense_id": "834c8751-365d-3225-a098-1eb843afb083",
                                "text": "[…] they had no sense of their condition; they were happy in a flowery, an arborous Sicilian garden: the volcano was below, and the giant earthquake only asleep."
                            },
